sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/turing-capable-network-topologies--claude-opus-5-5--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Sign-pattern theorem via additive D-stability and sign stability" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/turing-capable-network-topologies> ;
    dct:description "Reformulate. With linearization J at a stable steady state and diagonal diffusion D ≥ 0, a Turing instability is J stable with J − k²D unstable for some k > 0. Absorbing k² into D, the pattern P is Turing-capable (all species may diffuse) iff some realization J of P is stable but not additively D-stable, that is, J − D is unstable for some nonnegative diagonal D (Cross 1978). Lemma A: sign-stable patterns, characterized combinatorially by Quirk–Ruppert and Jeffries–Klee–van den Driessche (nonpositive diagonal, no positive 2-cycles, no cycles of length ≥ 3, nonzero determinant, a colour test), stay sign-stable when negative diagonal is added, hence are Turing-incapable. Conjecture B for n = 3: P is Turing-capable iff P is potentially stable and not sign-stable. Prove B by case analysis over which Jeffries condition fails (a 3-cycle, a positive self-loop, a mutualistic 2-cycle, or the colour test). For each case give an explicit parametric family (J(ε), D) that is stable, satisfying the 3×3 Routh–Hurwitz conditions a₁ > 0, a₃ > 0, a₁a₂ > a₃, with det(J − D) of the wrong sign or Routh–Hurwitz violated for J − D. For m < n diffusing species, D is supported on the diffusing set S, and the analogous criterion involves principal submatrices of J off S (Satnoianu et al. 2000)." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "A Lean-checked theorem: for n = 3 and each diffusing set S, the Turing-capable sign patterns are exactly those satisfying an explicit combinatorial condition (conjecturally 'potentially stable and not S-restricted sign-stable'), with zero disagreements against the exhaustive enumeration." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The enumeration finds a potentially stable, non-sign-stable pattern that is Turing-incapable (every stable realization is additively D-stable without being sign-stable), so Conjecture B is false and the characterization needs a finer invariant." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/proof" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Prove in Lean: for 3×3 real matrices, define stability by the Routh–Hurwitz inequalities on the characteristic polynomial coefficients, and prove that the Turing condition is equivalent to 'not additively D-stable'. 2. Prove Lemma A (sign-stable implies Turing-incapable) from the Jeffries conditions. 3. For each failure mode of sign stability, construct witness families and prove the inequalities with nlinarith or polyrith. 4. Extend to restricted diffusion sets S ⊂ {1,2,3} and state the theorem for each m. 5. Check the theorem against approach 2's enumeration (any disagreement is a counterexample to B)." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Mathlib lacks a ready Routh–Hurwitz theorem connecting coefficient inequalities to root location; for n = 3 it must be proved, or stability defined by the coefficient conditions with that equivalence proved separately." ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:note "Tool: mathlib" ;
    skos:note "Tool: sign-pattern-matrices" ;
    skos:note "Tool: linear-algebra" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-wavelength> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-morphogen-hypothesis> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/0024-3795(78)90021-6> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.4153/CJM-1977-035-3> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.2307/2295838> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1007/s002850000056> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/turing-capable-network-topologies> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Classify the network topologies that admit diffusion-driven instability" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> dct:title "The chemical basis of morphogenesis" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Turing 1952, The chemical basis of morphogenesis" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/0024-3795(78)90021-6> dct:title "Three types of matrix stability" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Cross 1978, Three types of matrix stability (D-stability, additive D-stability)" .
  <https://doi.org/10.4153/CJM-1977-035-3> dct:title "When is a Matrix Sign Stable?" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Jeffries, Klee and van den Driessche 1977, When is a matrix sign stable?" .
  <https://doi.org/10.2307/2295838> dct:title "Qualitative Economics and the Stability of Equilibrium" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Quirk and Ruppert 1965, Qualitative economics and the stability of equilibrium" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1007/s002850000056> dct:title "Turing instabilities in general systems" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Satnoianu, Menzinger and Maini 2000, Turing instabilities in general systems" .
}

